    "message": {
     "content": "**Yes, you should take it.** Financially, this is an exceptional outcome and puts you at the very top of Google\u2019s L6 PM band.\n\nYour negotiation was highly effective. By asking to cover your unvested Meta equity, you secured a **$200,000 cash sign-on bonus** on top of Google\u2019s already front-loaded equity schedule, matched your base salary, and boosted your target bonus percentage.\n\n---\n\n### The Numbers: How Your Earnings Look Now\n\nBecause Google vests equity **33% in Year 1, 33% in Year 2, 22% in Year 3, and 12% in Year 4**, your front-loaded compensation is extraordinary:\n\n| Component | Current Meta | Google Year 1 | Google Year 2 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 |\n| **Target Bonus** | $36,000 (15%) | $48,000 (20%) | $48,000 (20%) |\n| **Vesting Equity** | $250,000 | **$356,400** (33%) | **$356,400** (33%) |\n| **Sign-On Bonus** | $0 | **$200,000** *(if paid Y1)* | $0 |\n| **Total Comp (TC)** | **~$526,000** | **~$844,400** | **~$644,400** + Refreshes |\n\n#### 2-Year Financial Comparison\n* **Meta (2 Years):** ~$1.05M\n* **Google (2 Years):** **~$1.49M**\n* **Net Financial Gain:** You are taking home **over $440,000 more** across your first two years at Google than you would at Meta.\n\n---\n\n### Why This is a \"Slam Dunk\" Deal\n\n1. **You Effectively Double-Dipped on Year 1 Equity:** Instead of just matching your unvested $200k with standard-vesting stock, Google gave you **$200k in guaranteed cash upfront** *plus* their standard Year 1 vest ($356k).\n2. **Top-of-Band Compensation:** Total Year 1 comp of **~$844k** is well into L7 (Director/Principal) territory for tech compensation, achieved at an L6 level.\n3. **No Further Leverage to Push:** When Google meets a specific walk-away threshold (the $200k unvested grant) and explicitly states \"this is our best/final offer,\" attempting another round of negotiation risks goodwill without any meaningful upside.\n\n---\n\n### Final Details to Verify Before You Sign\n\n1. **Sign-On Distribution & Clawback:**\n   * Clarify whether the $200k is paid in a **single lump sum on your first paycheck** or split over two years (e.g., $100k in Year 1, $100k in Year 2). \n   * Verify the repayment terms (typically, leaving within 12 months requires a pro-rated return).\n2. **Start Date & Timing:**\n   * Time your departure from Meta so you don\u2019t forfeit a Meta vest that happens to fall just days before your start date. If a quarterly Meta vest is imminent, push your Google start date out slightly to capture it.\n\n---\n\n### The Verdict\n\nFrom a pure compensation and risk-adjusted return perspective, **accept the offer**. The only reason to decline at this point would be strictly non-financial (e.g., if you dislike the specific product team/scope in SF or strongly prefer Meta's product culture).",
